msgid "A role can have conditions in EventCrew > Settings: how many tasks of which roles a member has completed. Meeting them does not give the role. You are told, by Telegram and by email, the first time someone meets a role's conditions and the first time someone is given a role. /eligible lists who meets the conditions of each role."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/OrganizerGuide.php:121
msgid "A role is a kind of job, for example Welcome or Clean. You set the roles in Settings: name, emoji, a short description, how many people, and when it starts and ends compared to the event."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/settings.php:293
msgid "A role ticked \"Only people with this role\" (a DJ, a VJ, a ceremony leader) is shown only to people given that role, on the crew page, in the bot and at the sales desk. Its tasks have no sign-up limit and are never posted on the Telegram group board. Give people the role on the People page, on the crew page Admin tab, or with /roles in the bot. With \"Add to every night\" ticked, every upcoming night gets one task of that role, including nights that already exist; unticking it later removes nothing."
msgstr ""

